(intransitive, followed by \"for\") To look thoroughly.", "tags": ["intransitive"], "examples": ["The police are searching for evidence in his flat."], "quotes": [{"text": "It sufficeth that they have once with care and fairness sifted the matter as far as they could, and searched into all the particulars.", "reference": "1689 (indicated as 1690), [John Locke], An Essay Concerning Humane Understanding. […], London: […] Eliz[abeth] Holt, for Thomas Basset, […], →OCLC:"}, {"text": "He tried to persuade Cicely to stay away from the ball-room for a fourth dance.[…]But she said she must go back, and when they joined the crowd again[…]she found her mother standing up before the seat on which she had sat all the evening searching anxiously for her with her eyes, and her father by her side.", "reference": "1909 September 9, Archibald Marshall [pseudonym; Arthur Hammond Marshall], chapter I, in The Squire’s Daughter, London: Methuen & Co. […], →OCLC:"}, {"text": "Investors face a quandary. Cash offers a return of virtually zero in many developed countries; government-bond yields may have risen in recent weeks but they are still unattractive. Equities have suffered two big bear markets since 2000 and are wobbling again. It is hardly surprising that pension funds, insurers and endowments are searching for new sources of return.", "reference": "2013 July 6, “The rise of smart beta”, in The Economist, volume 408, number 8843, page 68:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "ar", "name": "Arabic"}, "word": "بَحَثَ عَنْ"}, {"language": {"code": "bn", "name": "Bengali"}, "word": "খোঁজা"}, {"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "търся"}, {"language": {"code": "my", "name": "Burmese"}, "word": "ရှာ"}, {"language": {"code": "ca", "name": "Catalan"}, "word": "buscar"}, {"language": {"code": "ca", "name": "Catalan"}, "word": "cercar"}, {"language": {"code": "cs", "name": "Czech"}, "word": "hledat"}, {"language": {"code": "da", "name